    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0354" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg254"/>

                <head>No. 179.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 11th
                    instant, I have the honor to inform you that the memorandum which accompanied
                    it, concerning the state of the labor traffic in the Western Pacific islands,
                    has received careful examination. This Government looks with favor upon any
                    humanitarian work, and would like more information as to the scope and form of
                    the proposed agreement.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
